= Practice Questions (Exam Pattern)

Ten questions designed in authentic CUET UG single-correct style. The official marking scheme awards $+5$ for each correct answer and deducts $-1$ for every incorrect answer.

#mcq(1, [In June 1991, roughly how much foreign exchange reserves remained with the Indian government, triggering the adoption of structural economic reforms?], (
  [Barely 2 weeks of imports], [Nearly 6 months of imports], [Over 1 year of imports], [Sufficient for 3 months of imports],
))

#mcq(2, [Which prominent farmers' leader led the Karnataka Rajya Raitha Sangha (KRRS) in militant direct actions against WTO patent regimes and multinational seed corporations?], (
  [Mahendra Singh Tikait], [Sharad Joshi], [M.D. Nanjundaswamy], [Chaudhary Charan Singh],
))

#mcq(3, [Which organization was founded by Kanshi Ram in 1978 as a non-political federation of government employees from backward and minority communities?], (
  [Dalit Shoshit Samaj Sangharsh Samiti (DS-4)], [Bahujan Samaj Party (BSP)], [BAMCEF], [Dalit Panthers],
))

#mcq(4, [The militant social organization 'Dalit Panthers' was founded in which Indian state in May 1972?], (
  [Uttar Pradesh], [Bihar], [Maharashtra], [Punjab],
))

#mcq(5, [Who among the following was a renowned Marathi poet and co-founder of the Dalit Panthers who authored the radical collection 'Golpitha'?], (
  [Namdeo Dhasal], [Kanshi Ram], [Ram Vilas Paswan], [B.R. Ambedkar],
))

#mcq(6, [In which year did the Faizabad District Court order the opening of the locks of the disputed Babri structure in Ayodhya to allow Hindu devotees to offer prayers?], (
  [1949], [1984], [1986], [1992],
))

#mcq(7, [Who was the Chief Minister of Uttar Pradesh who resigned immediately following the demolition of the Babri Masjid on 6 December 1992?], (
  [Mulayam Singh Yadav], [Kalyan Singh], [Mayawati], [Rajnath Singh],
))

#mcq(8, [Which judicial inquiry commission was appointed by the Government of India in December 1992 to investigate the sequence of events leading to the demolition of the Babri Masjid?], (
  [Shah Commission], [Liberhan Commission], [Sarkaria Commission], [Nanavati Commission],
))

#mcq(9, [In which landmark judgment did the Supreme Court uphold the dismissal of four BJP state governments in 1992, ruling that 'Secularism is part of the Basic Structure'?], (
  [Kesavananda Bharati Case (1973)], [Indra Sawhney Case (1992)], [S.R. Bommai Case (1994)], [Minerva Mills Case (1980)],
))

#mcq(10, [Following the communal violence in Gujarat in 2002, the Supreme Court famously transferred which high-profile riot trial outside Gujarat to Maharashtra?], (
