))

= Detailed Solutions

#solution(1, [By June 1991, India's foreign currency reserves dropped to barely \$1.2 billion, adequate for only about two weeks of essential imports, forcing structural LPG economic reforms.], answer: [A])

#solution(2, [Prof. M.D. Nanjundaswamy led the Karnataka Rajya Raitha Sangha (KRRS) in high-profile agitations against WTO intellectual property rules, multinational corporations, and seed patenting.], answer: [C])

#solution(3, [Kanshi Ram established BAMCEF (Backward and Minority Communities Employees Federation) in 1978 as a non-electoral body of salaried public sector employees to build an intellectual and financial base.], answer: [C])

#solution(4, [The Dalit Panthers was founded in Maharashtra (specifically in the slums of Bombay) in May 1972 by young writers and activists resisting entrenched rural caste atrocities.], answer: [C])

#solution(5, [Namdeo Dhasal, a pathbreaking Marathi poet who wrote 'Golpitha', co-founded the Dalit Panthers alongside J.V. Pawar and Arjun Dangle in 1972.], answer: [A])

#solution(6, [In February 1986, the Faizabad District Judge ordered the locks of the Babri structure opened for Hindu worship, an event that escalated religious mobilization on both sides.], answer: [C])

#solution(7, [Kalyan Singh headed the BJP state government in Uttar Pradesh; he submitted his resignation to the Governor on the evening of 6 December 1992 after the structure was demolished.], answer: [B])

#solution(8, [The Justice M.S. Liberhan Commission of Inquiry was constituted in December 1992 to probe the Babri Masjid demolition; it submitted its findings in 2009.], answer: [B])

#solution(9, [In S.R. Bommai vs Union of India (1994), a nine-judge constitutional bench ruled that secularism is a fundamental feature of the basic structure, validating the dismissal of four state governments.], answer: [C])

#solution(10, [In the Best Bakery Case (Vadodara), the Supreme Court ordered a retrial outside Gujarat in Maharashtra to ensure fair, uninfluenced proceedings for victim-witness Zahira Sheikh.], answer: [B])

